            <ArticleTitle>Endovascular aneurysm repair for multiple aneurysms as a sequel of hypereosinophilic syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>277-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1538574413518610</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case represents the first report of multiple arterial aneurysms including aortic, iliac, visceral, and coronary aneurysms associated with hypereosinophilic syndrome. It presents an interesting case of epinephrine abuse and the unfortunate sequelae. This case illustrates novel approaches in emergency repair of internal iliac artery aneurysm rupture and the management of visceral artery aneurysms and exemplifies how multiple endovascular technologies can be utilized even in the high-risk polymorbid patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
